# Kotlin and Compose

Kotlin only. Do not add Java source.

Follow the official Kotlin style (`kotlin.code.style=official`).

## Compose

- Keep state in the caller. Composables receive state and event callbacks.
- UI logic stays in the composable. Data loading does not.
- Add a `@Preview` when a composable has a real layout. Skip previews for one-line placeholders.
- Material 3. Adaptive layout rules live in `layout-standards.mdc`.

## Structure

Single `app` module. Add a package only when a feature arrives: `ui`, then `weather`, `radar`, and `data`.

Do not add Hilt, extra modules, or a repository interface until a second implementation needs it.

Coroutines and Flow are the async tools once a feature needs them. Do not add them for unused scaffolding.
